# ⌊%tid.x/3⌋ written as LLVM writes a division by a constant that is no
# power of two, the upper half of a product by a magic number and a
# shift: the tracer reads no mul.hi, and the address is unknown (PLAN,
# "Addresses the tracer cannot read").
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/magic_div.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_magic_div
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
CHECK-SAME: unknown: `mul.hi.u32` keeps a product's upper half
